    <td align="left" vAlign="top" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;
		<table align="left" border="0" cellPadding="1" cellSpacing="1" width="100%" bgcolor="#000000">
        
			<tr>
				<td style="WIDTH: 15px" width="15"></td>
				<td align="left" class="TextMain" bgcolor="#000000">
					<center><h2>Rules And Conduct For GPK</h2></center>

					What are GPKs?
					<BR><BR>
					GPK's are in-guild currency used for the »purchasing« of loot that drops on guild run 
					raids. As the abbreviation » guild participation kredits« hints these are gained by 
					taking part on guild raids or other events including helping fellow guildies obtaining 
					their epics. This system is used to promote guild participation and to eliminate so 
					called bad lottos, that is items being won by players that have no real use for 
					them. GPKs are only taken into account if at least 2 full groups are on the raid.
					<BR><BR>
					Earning GPKs
					<BR><BR>
					GPKs are awarded for participating in guild raids or other events. Each encounter 
					is valued separately based upon the difficulty of the mob and several other 
					factors. You can see the value of each individual encounter in the » encounter 
					chart«. The values there are prone to change when some encounters get trivial 
					for us or we target new mobs to kill or the encounters listed are found harder 
					that the amount of allocated GPKs hint. GPKs are only given for encounters listed 
					in encounter chart. Other events may also be given GPK status and value if 
					Firius/Garaddor personally approve it. Raid leaders of GPK raids are expected 
					to keep track of the people who have attended raid and how many GPKs they have 
					earned during that raid. Players are requested to inform raid leaders of their 
					time of arrival and time of departure on and from that raid. Raid leader is then 
					expected to post the amount of GPKs earned by each individual on the appropriate 
					section of our website. There is a chart on our website displaying the amount of 
					GPK that each member possesses and is updated within a few days of each GPK 
					earning event. 


					<BR><BR>
					Using GPKs to acquire items 
					<BR><BR>
					Items are distributed by means of an auction where GPKs are used as currency. The 
					class that can use the item »their class name is listed on the item« and is on 
					the raid »has been in a fight to kill the mob« can enter the auction. The player 
					offering most GPKs for the item loots the item. Items that cannot be used by 
					anyone on raid or no one bids on them are saved in ADD guildbank and are on auction 
					for main characters only for 3 days after the raid. After those 3 days are up 
					the items are on auction for any character (including lvl 1 twinks if anyone 
					wishes) for another 3 days. Items that are not wanted even then are kept by guild 
					to be sold in market to finance cleric gems and wizard port stones. Armor quest 
					gems that drop during raid are saved in ADD guildbank and are given freely to 
					anyone in guild that has obtained required piece of armor and has high enough 
					faction. If loot drops that only one person on raid can use then no auction 
					takes place and if the player wants and will use that item they pay a set amount 
					of GPK for it even if it pushes his account into negative. If two people bid the 
					same amount of GPK for an item, then only the first bid is valid. You must bid 
					one GPK higher for an item as ties are not allowed. 

					<BR><BR>
					How many GPKs do I have to spend?
					<BR><BR>
					While the officers will try to keep a current tally of what each player has to 
					spend, it is the responsibility of each player to check the web site for their 
					current total and keep their own running total of what they have available to 
					spend. The amount of GPKs each person can use on a specific raid is the amount 
					of GPK that person had at the start of that day. That means if the person had 
					120 GPK at start of the day and has been on 2 raids earning an additional 25 
					GPKs they can still only use 120 GPKs (minus any spending) on the eventual 3rd 
					raid. GPKs earned during that raid day will not be taken into account until the 
					next update to the guild web site. However, any GPK spending must be deducted 
					from the last web site total and a player cannot spend more than they currently 
					have after deducting for any recent GPK spending.

					<BR><BR>
					Epic Items
					<BR><BR>
					Epic items that drop are given for the price of 1 GPK to players with most career 
					GPK points present on raid. 

					<BR><BR>
					What happens if out of guild people/friends join the raids? 
					<BR><BR>
					In that case the person rolls against everyone in our guild that can and will 
					use the item. If that person wins the roll he naturally loots the item. If that 
					person/persons lose the roll then auction takes place as if the other people were 
					not on raid. 

					<BR><BR>
					Who can participate in auctions? 
					<BR><BR>
					Items are auctioned on by players who can use the item (their class/race is listed 
					on the item) and they have positive number of GPKs (their account is not in negative 
					figures). If no one on raid can use the item it goes to guildbank and is treated as 
					described above. 

					<BR><BR>
					What if someone has more than one character in the guild? 
					<BR><BR>
					GPKs are earned by each RL person and not by individual characters or accounts. All 
					character GPKs will be tracked under one “main” character name. You cannot bid for 
					one of your other characters if that character is not there at the raid. So take the 
					character you wish to get loot with to the raid. In rare situations, the raid leader 
					may deem a certain class is needed to enhance the potential success of the raid. For 
					this situation, the raid leader can approve bidding for a character not at the raid 
					if that person will be playing their other character needed for the raid. The person 
					can only bid for one character and can not bid for the character at the raid if they 
					had decided in advance to bid for a different character. The characters must be in 
					ADD and of appropriate level for the raid for this situation to apply. If someone is 
					playing two characters at a raid, then either character may bid on items, but GPKs 
					are earned once (per one RL person, not each character) under the ‘main’ character’s 
					name. 

					<BR><BR>
					Exceptions to auction system 
					<BR><BR>
					Exceptions to auction system arise when it is clear that an individual has »earned« a 
					specific item. »Earning« would mean that an individual has spent large amounts of time 
					waiting for the mob to pop and is instrumental in reserving that mob until a successful 
					kill by ADD. Example would be camping Lodizal for long periods of time with intent to 
					obtain map piece or shell used in shield quest. The person must state well before the 
					mob pops which item he/she is after. If that item does not drop when the mob is killed 
					the auction takes place as if there were no special circumstances. If that item does 
					drop though the person pays a preset amount of GPKs and loots it without an auction 
					taking place on that specific item. 					
					<BR><BR><br>
				</td>
				<td style="WIDTH: 15px" width="15"></td></tr>
